# Living rebuild plan

Before planning or implementing, read [`README.md`](README.md). That file is the plan. New boards follow README **Adding a board** (pioarduino + `BOARD_PROFILE_*`). The PDF in the repo root is historical only. Do not copy its `platformio.ini` starter (`qspi_opi`, 8MB partitions, SDMMC, huge rings). Queued C5/C6/P4/`NetIf`/catalog work is listed under README **Multi-board**; see also [`.cursor/rules/multi-board.mdc`](multi-board.mdc).

## Checklist

- Mark `[x]` when the code is in the tree.
- Mark `[x] **verified**` only after the user confirms it on hardware.
- **Never delete** a list item, including completed ones.
- **Never uncheck** a **verified** item unless the user asks.
- Add new lines when scope grows; do not rewrite history by removing old ones.

Share `src/` across boards. Add a PlatformIO env and board profile for other ESP32 / MCU variants instead of forking.
